\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The protected class, globally. $\qopname  \relax o{log}_{10}\|[C(s_{\mathrm  {ref}}), C(s)]\|$ over the shape torus, with $s_{\mathrm  {ref}}$ the first C15 pair's first shape (star). An exhaustive basin-polished scan finds exactly two zeros: the reference and one isolated level partner (circle, 1.057\,rad away) with $C = C_{\mathrm  {ref}}$ --- the discrete level set on which holonomy protection is exact at all orders.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:heatmap}{{3}{3}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Distributions behind the summary numbers. (a)\nobreakspace  {}Empirical CDF of the per-draw remainder constant $\qopname  \relax m{sup}_\tau \|R\|/\tau ^3$ over 220 shape draws; the quoted 0.0133 is the supremum. (b)\nobreakspace  {}All 20 per-formation slopes: support width $3\times 10^{-13}$.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:remstats}{{4}{4}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Bound tightness. (a)\nobreakspace  {}Measured amplitude vs.\ the leading-order prediction $\tau ^2\|[C_i,C_j]\|$, 60 draws $\times $ 4 stalenesses, on the identity line. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Measured/predicted ratio $\to 1$ as $\tau \to 0$; the 5--95\% band across draws is narrower than $2\times 10^{-4}$.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bound}{{5}{4}}
